From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun Gupta <varun.gupta@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0530
Subject: drm/pagemap: use page->pgmap when struct folio has no pgmap

On kernels without page_pgmap(), struct folio does not carry a direct
pgmap pointer. When folios are split, preserve pgmap by copying from
the head page field.

This keeps folio split metadata propagation correct on backported-THP
bases where folio_split exists but folio->pgmap does not.

Reference:
	82ba975e4c43
	mm: allow compound zone device pages

Signed-off-by: Varun Gupta <varun.gupta@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c
index 5b362f2..2ce35d1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c
@@ -1302,7 +1302,15 @@ static void drm_pagemap_folio_split(struct folio *orig_folio, struct folio *new_
 	if (!new_folio)
 		return;
 
+#ifdef BPM_PAGE_PGMAP_NOT_PRESENT
+	/*
+	 * struct folio has no pgmap on kernels without page_pgmap();
+	 * use the head page's.
+	 */
+	new_folio->page.pgmap = orig_folio->page.pgmap;
+#else
 	new_folio->pgmap = orig_folio->pgmap;
+#endif
 	zdd = folio_zone_device_data(orig_folio);
 	folio_set_zone_device_data(new_folio, drm_pagemap_zdd_get(zdd));
 }
